# Production build configuration, read by Vite for `npm run build`.
#
# Committed on purpose. These are not secrets: a browser app has to ship its user
# pool and client id in order to sign anyone in, so they are readable in the bundle
# by anyone who can load the page. The client is configured with no secret for
# exactly that reason - see cdk/lib/cognito_stack.py.
#
# A file rather than shell exports so the deployed build cannot quietly lose its
# login screen. `npm run build` picks these up with no operator action; leaving it
# to the environment means one forgotten export ships a bundle where
# isAuthConfigured is false and the app renders with no sign-in at all - which
# still "works" against CloudFront because API Gateway would 401 every call, so it
# presents as a broken API rather than a missing login.
#
# Deliberately NOT a plain `.env`, which would also apply to `npm run dev`. Local
# development runs against `uvicorn` with no API Gateway authorizer in front of it.
#
# Values are the deployed dev stack: the pool is shared with the marketing tool,
# the client id is this app's own (PlanningRoadmap-dev CognitoStack).
VITE_COGNITO_USER_POOL_ID=ca-central-1_P8orSDvVO
VITE_COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=pciat37670n002pk5ji276k27
VITE_AWS_REGION=ca-central-1
